Display management tools for X11 (xrandr) and Plasma's native kscreen-doctor.

@text
xrandr — X11 Display Configuration

@code bash
# List all outputs and supported modes
xrandr

# List outputs with verbose mode details
xrandr --verbose

# Set resolution for a specific output
xrandr --output HDMI-1 --mode 1920x1080

# Set resolution and refresh rate
xrandr --output HDMI-1 --mode 2560x1440 --rate 144

# Enable a second monitor to the right of primary
xrandr --output HDMI-1 --mode 1920x1080 --right-of eDP-1

# Mirror displays
xrandr --output HDMI-1 --same-as eDP-1

# Set primary display
xrandr --output eDP-1 --primary

# Disable an output
xrandr --output HDMI-1 --off

# Rotate a display
xrandr --output HDMI-1 --rotate left    # left, right, inverted, normal

# Set a custom mode (add modeline)
cvt 1920 1080 60                        # generate modeline
xrandr --newmode "1920x1080_60" 173.00 1920 2048 2248 2576 1080 1083 1088 1120 -hsync +vsync
xrandr --addmode HDMI-1 "1920x1080_60"
xrandr --output HDMI-1 --mode "1920x1080_60"

# Set brightness (software, 0.0-1.0)
xrandr --output eDP-1 --brightness 0.8

@text
kscreen-doctor — Plasma Native Display Tool

Works with both X11 and Wayland sessions. Respects Plasma's display configuration.

@code bash
# Show current display configuration
kscreen-doctor --outputs

# Enable an output at a specific mode
kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-1.enable output.HDMI-1.mode.1920x1080@60

# Disable an output
kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-1.disable

# Set position (x,y from top-left)
kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-1.position.1920,0

# Set as primary
kscreen-doctor output.eDP-1.primary

# Set rotation
kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-1.rotation.left   # none, left, right, inverted

# Set scale (Wayland)
kscreen-doctor output.eDP-1.scale.1.5

# Combined: enable, position, and set mode
kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-1.enable \
  output.HDMI-1.mode.2560x1440@144 \
  output.HDMI-1.position.1920,0

@text
DPI and Scaling

Configure HiDPI scaling for Plasma and applications.

@code bash
# Set global scale factor (Plasma 5, integer scaling)
kwriteconfig5 --file kdeglobals --group KScreen --key ScaleFactor 2

# Set per-screen Wayland scaling (Plasma 6 supports fractional)
kscreen-doctor output.eDP-1.scale.1.25

# Force-set DPI for X11
xrandr --dpi 192

# Set font DPI (affects font rendering size)
kwriteconfig5 --file kcmfonts --group General --key forceFontDPI 144

# Environment variables for app scaling
# Add to ~/.xprofile or ~/.profile:
# export QT_AUTO_SCREEN_SCALE_FACTOR=1     # Qt apps auto-detect
# export QT_SCALE_FACTOR=1.5               # Force Qt scale
# export GDK_SCALE=2                        # GTK integer scale
# export GDK_DPI_SCALE=0.5                  # GTK DPI compensation
# export PLASMA_USE_QT_SCALING=1            # Plasma 6 fractional

@text
Multi-Monitor Layout

@code bash
# Common layouts with xrandr:
# Side-by-side (laptop left, external right)
xrandr --output eDP-1 --primary --mode 1920x1080 --pos 0x0 \
       --output HDMI-1 --mode 2560x1440 --pos 1920x0

# Stacked (external above laptop)
xrandr --output eDP-1 --primary --mode 1920x1080 --pos 0x1440 \
       --output HDMI-1 --mode 2560x1440 --pos 0x0

# Only external (laptop lid closed)
xrandr --output eDP-1 --off --output HDMI-1 --primary --auto

# Plasma saves display configs per connected set:
# ~/.local/share/kscreen/   — stored layouts, auto-applied on connect

# Force reload saved kscreen config
kscreen-doctor --dpms on

@text
DPMS — Display Power Management

@code bash
# Check DPMS status
xset q | grep -A5 "DPMS"

# Turn off display immediately
xset dpms force off

# Turn on display
xset dpms force on

# Set standby/suspend/off timeouts (seconds)
xset dpms 300 600 900

# Disable DPMS entirely
xset -dpms

# Prevent screen blanking
xset s off s noblank
